{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:109-110", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "109-110"}, "paraphrase": "Posture destroys disease, prāṇāyāma sin, pratyāhāra mental disturbance; dhāraṇā gives steadiness of mind, samādhi the wonderful consciousness and liberation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:dhyanabindu-six-limbs"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:111-112", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "111-112"}, "paraphrase": "Twelve prāṇāyāmas make a pratyāhāra, twelve pratyāhāras a dhāraṇā, twelve dhāraṇās a dhyāna, twelve dhyānas a samādhi.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:yogacudamani-twelvefold-ladder"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:114-115", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "114-115"}, "paraphrase": "Closing the senses (the ṣaṇmukhī) the yogin hears sounds like bells within.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:shanmukhi-mudra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:116-118", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "116-118"}, "paraphrase": "Proper prāṇāyāma destroys all disease; improper practice produces hiccup, asthma, cough, pains of head, ears and eyes. As a lion, elephant or tiger is tamed slowly, breath must be controlled gradually, otherwise it kills the practitioner.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "obstacles": ["obs:improper-pranayama"], "practices": ["prc:nadi-sodhana"], "cross_refs": ["tea:sandilya-upanisad:1.23"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:2-3", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2-3"}, "paraphrase": "Posture, breath-restraint, withdrawal, concentration, meditation and absorption are the six limbs of yoga; of postures siddha and kamala (lotus) are chief. The yogin should know the six centres, sixteen supports (ādhāra), three targets (lakṣya) and five voids (vyoma).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "paths": ["pth:dhyanabindu-six-limbs"], "concepts": ["cpt:cakras", "cpt:three-laksyas", "cpt:vyoma-pancaka"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:27-30", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "27-30"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva is tossed up and down by prāṇa and apāna like a ball struck by the bat, and like a hawk tied by a string it is drawn back.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "cross_refs": ["tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:58-60"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:31-35", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "31-35"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva repeats the ajapā-gāyatrī 21,600 times a day; it arises from the kuṇḍalinī; it is the knowledge of prāṇa and the great knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:ajapa-gayatri"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:43-44", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "43-44"}, "paraphrase": "Moderate diet is food that is sweet and unctuous, leaving a quarter of the stomach empty, eaten for Śiva's pleasure. The kuṇḍalinī is bondage for the ignorant and liberation for yogins.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:mitahara"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:71-88", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "71-88"}, "paraphrase": "Praṇava and the four states; sa means 'you' and ha 'that' — their union is 'that you are'; bound by the senses and 'mine' one is jīva, by 'not mine' kevala; one who repeats the praṇava, pure or impure, is untouched like a lotus leaf by water.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras", "cpt:hamsa"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogacudamani-upanisad:98-99", "source": "src:yogacudamani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "98-99"}, "paraphrase": "Signs of purified channels: breath held at will, stronger digestive fire, the inner sound manifest, and health.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "practices": ["prc:nadi-sodhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
